  "id": "houston",
  "intro": "Houston gives you two things at unusual scale. The Ship Channel is the busiest petrochemical waterway in the country, and its Vessel Traffic Service — running from Galveston Bay up to the Turning Basin — is genuinely gripping to follow. Severe weather here is on another level, so the NOAA transmitters and the amateur SKYWARN nets matter more than almost anywhere else: in hurricane season this is the region where a handheld stops being a hobby. Add two major airports, a working freight port and the most humid VHF conditions in the country, and there is always something on.",
  "introz": "德州有三样规模异常的东西。休斯顿航道是全美最繁忙的石化水道，它的船舶交通管理服务听起来相当扣人心弦。这里的恶劣天气完全是另一个量级，所以 NOAA 发射台和业余 SKYWARN 通联网比几乎任何地方都重要。而圣安东尼奥周边一圈空军基地在军用 AM 波段上产生大量训练通话，VX-6 正好能覆盖。",
  "stations": [
    { "f": 156.550, "n": "Houston Ship Channel VTS — Ch 11", "z": "休斯顿航道交管 11 频道", "c": "marine", "m": "NFM", "conf": "check", "a": "Houston Ship Channel & Galveston Bay", "d": "A narrow, crowded, fifty-mile channel carrying tankers and chemical ships past refineries, with pilots, tugs and traffic control coordinating continuously. Set up near the Fred Hartman Bridge or the Lynchburg ferry and this becomes some of the most absorbing radio in the country. Scan 156.300–157.400 to find the sector in use.", "dz": "一条狭窄拥挤、长约五十英里的航道，油轮和化学品船穿行于炼油厂之间，引航员、拖轮和交通管制持续协调。在 Fred Hartman 桥或 Lynchburg 渡口附近守听，这会成为全美最令人入迷的无线电内容之一。扫 156.300–157.400 找当前在用的分区。", "odds": 2 },
