    { "f": 146.940, "n": "SKYWARN net repeater", "z": "SKYWARN 风暴观测网中继", "c": "ham", "m": "FM", "conf": "check", "o": "−0.600", "t": "110.9", "a": "Repeaters", "d": "Texas has one of the most developed amateur storm-spotter networks in the world. When a supercell is approaching, the SKYWARN net on a local repeater gives you eyewitness reports of rotation and hail size well before any warning is issued. This is the single best argument for carrying a radio in Texas. Check RepeaterBook and your county ARES page for the active net frequency.", "dz": "德州拥有全球最成熟的业余风暴观测网络之一。超级单体来临时，本地中继上的 SKYWARN 通联网会在正式警报发布之前就给出目击者对旋转和冰雹尺寸的报告。这是在德州带一台电台最有力的理由。请在 RepeaterBook 和所在县的 ARES 页面查当前通联网频率。", "odds": 2 },
